-- title:
--   Integral closedness from a crossing presentation gh=varpi^ew
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring in the Mathlib sense) and let $R$ be a noetherian local commutative domain equipped with an $O$-algebra structure. Let $\varpi \in O$ be irreducible, and assume that the composite $O \to R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ of the structure map with the residue map is surjective, so that the residue field of $R$ is generated by the image of $O$. Let $g, h, w \in R$ with $w$ a unit, and let $e \ge 1$ be a natural number such that $g h = \varpi^{e} w$, where $\varpi$ denotes its image in $R$. Assume further that the maximal ideal of $R$ is the ideal generated by $\varpi$, $g$ and $h$; that the ideals $(\varpi, g)$ and $(\varpi, h)$ are both prime; that $h \notin (\varpi, g)$ and $g \notin (\varpi, h)$; and that $2$ is a unit in $R$. Then $R$ is integrally closed in its field of fractions.
--
--   This is the local criterion identifying a ring with an $A_{e-1}$-type crossing presentation over a discrete valuation ring as normal; it is applied at the points where two branches meet. It is used in the analysis of local rings of modular curves, namely by [`ModularCurve.eq_of_isPrime_of_liesOver_descendedNodeRing_of_ne_zero_of_ne_1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eq_of_isPrime_of_liesOver_descendedNodeRing_of_ne_zero_of_ne_1728), [`ModularCurve.isIntegrallyClosed_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isIntegrallyClosed_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring) and [`ModularCurve.isIntegrallyClosed_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_ne_zero_of_ne_1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isIntegrallyClosed_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_ne_zero_of_ne_1728).
